{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Adding a GeoJSON file to the map","anchor":"Adding-a-GeoJSON-file-to-the-map","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MapLibre iOS offers several ways to work with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/geojson.org\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" files."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON is a standard file format for representing geographic data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can host a GeoJSON file or bundle it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your application, you can use a GeoJSON file as the basis of an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object. Pass the file’s URL into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:URL:options:","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" initializer and add the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape source to the map using the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNStyle\/addSource:","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. The URL may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be a local file URL, an HTTP URL, or an HTTPS URL."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you’ve added the GeoJSON file to the map via an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" object,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can configure the appearance of its data and control what data is visible"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" objects. You can also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"#Extracting-GeoJSON-data-from-the-map","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Converting GeoJSON data into shape objects","anchor":"Converting-GeoJSON-data-into-shape-objects","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you have GeoJSON data in the form of source code (also known as “GeoJSON"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text”), you can convert it into an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNFeature","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeCollectionFeature","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" object that the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" class understands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"natively. First, create an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSData"},{"type":"text","text":" object out of the source code string or file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contents, then pass that data object into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape\/shapeWithData:encoding:error:","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. Finally, you can pass the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resulting shape or feature object into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:shape:options:","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" initializer and add it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the map, or you can use the object and its properties to power non-map-related"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functionality in your application."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To include multiple shapes in the source, create and pass an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeCollection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeCollectionFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" object to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:shape:options:"},{"text":". Alternatively, use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:features:options:","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:shapes:options:","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method to create a shape source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with an array. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:features:options:","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" accepts only ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instances, such